thomask@lynx.cs.washington.edu (Thomas K. Schonhoff) writes:

>OK, this is probably heresy but just how (if at all) can I get RID of an
>intrinsic I don't really want?  In the most recent case I ate a leprechaun
>and can't stop jumping...  Worse was the time I ate a stalker (and the time
>I drank a blessed potion of invisibility) and became permanently invisible
>which was great until I wanted something from a shop...

Have a gremlin hit you (this will only work at night: 21:00 - 06:00)
and you have a one-in-ten chance that you will lose a random intrinsic.
Don't expect to lose the one you WANT to get rid of the first time,
though. You'll probably lose some other intrinsics as well (I wouldn't
mind losing aggravate monster, but this is unfortunately not possible:
see below...).

As far as I know, this is the only way to lose an intrinsic. The
intrinsics you can lose this way are:

Intrinsic lost		Message
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~	~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
fire resistance		You feel warmer.
teleportation		You feel less jumpy.
poison resistance	You feel a little sick!
telepathy		Your senses fail!
cold resistance		You feel cooler.
invisibility		You feel paranoid.
see invisible		You thought you saw something!
speed			You feel slower.
stealth			You feel clumsy.
protection		You feel vulnerable.

Note that the chance of losing an intrinsic is pretty slim, unless you
are facing hundreds of gremlins at the same time, which is possible if
there is a lot of water nearby.

First, a gremlin gets four attacks, only the last of which can remove
an intrinsic. Then, this last attack must hit you. If it hits, you have
a one-in-ten chance that you might lose an intrinsic. The game randomly
chooses one from the above list, and if you have that intrinsic, you
lose it.

